// D15569: a width-generic integer intrinsic named as a value takes the width its destination's
// function type names, so an i64 destination reads i64 `clz`, equal to `clz(x as i64)`.
// The un-annotated face and `return_inferred` pin nothing, so they read the default width by
// the same ruling: an i64 argument does not narrow to i32, so that face refuses at check.
//
// Format: scripts/capability-probes/README.md, "Template format".
// @@VALUE@@
clz
// @@TYPE@@
(i64) => i64
// @@TEST@@
v(1 as i64) == (63 as i64)
// @@HIT@@
print(v(256 as i64))
// @@MISS@@
print("miss")
// @@WANT@@
55
